    description: "FOUND 2026-09-23 while closing INV-zikab. This is the shape INV-zikab step 6 blocked for the JDK statics, and it already exists for scala's own owned function rows.\n\nMEASURED on gatling (survey at 9a81416ad6, production classify_call with dst_ref): 11 call edges with NO call_construct and an `external` slot classify as scala.io.StdIn reads. They are LogFileReader's OWN parser methods: readInt x6, readBoolean x3, readLong x1, readByte x1 (gatling-charts/.../stats/LogFileReader.scala:131, 136, 152, 202). They are false stdin reads: the same class defines readString, which INV-zikab step 6's arm B matched as Files.readString.\n\nMECHANISM: gate_named_entry (the no-module-context path) matches any function-kind row by bare name unless the name is in ambiguous_names. scala.io.StdIn's members are owned (`StdIn.readInt()`); a bare `readInt()` reaches them legitimately only via `import scala.io.StdIn._`. Predef's bare readInt/readLine were deprecated in 2.11 and removed in 2.13.\n\nTHE TRADE, NOT YET MEASURED: listing them in ambiguous_names removes these FPs and also drops genuine `import scala.io.StdIn._; readInt()` calls. Measure both on a scala cohort before choosing. The scala.io.Source rows (fromFile, fromURL, ...) have the same exposure; no FP was seen in sbt/http4s/gatling."  # 12af
    fields: {}  # 12af
